      "sourceTextSha256": "ec88e67ec09e97e4bf9e9a11ee30049bebbc007d20d51f33888f49687f25f117",
      "text": "Today you have a full-day excursion. The drive to the main area takes about **2–3 hours**. In the evening, check in at your hotel in Purmamarca.\n\nUNESCO recognises the Quebrada de Humahuaca for its cultural landscape. People have lived in this area for more than 10,000 years. Indigenous fortresses, prehistoric caves, farmsteads, and pre-Columbian and colonial settlements survive here.\n\nIn Purmamarca, you’ll see the Hill of Seven Colours, the Sierra de los Siete Colores, and the historic church of Santa Rosa de Lima.\n\nContinue to Tilcara to visit an ancient Indigenous fortress. Along the way, see Uquía and its church, which houses a collection of paintings of the Angels with Arquebuses.\n\nIn Humahuaca, you can walk along old cobbled streets and see colonial-era landmarks. The town stands on the banks of the Río Grande.",
